id: rust.retry
kind: rust
title: Retries with exponential backoff
aliases: retry, backoff, jitter
tags: resilience, async
questions:
  - how do you implement retries correctly?
invariant: Retry only idempotent operations, with exponential backoff plus jitter, a bounded attempt count and a total deadline.
answer_30s: Retry idempotent calls with exponential backoff and jitter, cap attempts and total time, and classify errors so permanent failures are not retried.
answer_2m: |
  Every ingredient has a reason. Idempotency: a timeout may mean the write
  succeeded. Backoff: an immediate retry amplifies load exactly when the
  dependency is struggling. Jitter: without it all clients retry in lockstep,
  which is the thundering herd that turns a blip into an outage. Caps: without
  them one slow call becomes a request holding a connection for minutes. Error
  classification: retrying a validation error just wastes budget. And if
  retries exist at two layers, cap the total -- layered retries multiply.
when_to_use:
  - transient network or dependency errors on idempotent operations
avoid_when:
  - non-idempotent writes without an idempotency key; validation or auth failures
minimal_example: |
  let mut delay = Duration::from_millis(50);
  for attempt in 1..=4 {
      match call().await {
          Ok(v) => return Ok(v),
          Err(e) if e.is_retryable() && attempt < 4 => {
              let jitter = Duration::from_millis(rand::random::<u64>() % 50);
              tokio::time::sleep(delay + jitter).await;
              delay *= 2;
          }
          Err(e) => return Err(e),
      }
  }
failure_modes:
  - retrying non-idempotent writes, creating duplicates
  - no jitter, so retries synchronise across clients
  - retries at two layers multiplying the effective attempt count
follow_ups:
  - what stops retries from making an overload worse?
related:
  - design.retry-backoff
  - design.idempotency
  - design.circuit-breaker
  - rust.timeout
  - recipe.resilient-dependent-service
sources:
  - https://aws.amazon.com/builders-library/timeouts-retries-and-backoff-with-jitter/
